1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,540
一座木建筑的屋檐，为什么能伸出柱子之外？
How can the eaves of a timber building extend beyond its columns?

2
00:00:04,540 --> 00:00:07,683
答案，就藏在梁思成的这张图里。
The answer lies in this drawing by Liang Sicheng.

3
00:00:08,683 --> 00:00:12,257
这页题为，中国建筑之，ORDER。
This page is titled The Chinese “Order”.

4
00:00:12,257 --> 00:00:15,200
它把斗拱、柱、柱础连成一体，
It brings brackets, columns and column bases into one system,

5
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:17,933
让我们从屋檐一路读到地面。
guiding our eye from the eaves down to the ground.

6
00:00:18,933 --> 00:00:21,942
先抓住一条线索：屋面的荷载，
Start with one clue: the load from the roof

7
00:00:21,942 --> 00:00:25,166
通过梁枋和斗拱等构件，传到柱，
passes through beams, ties and brackets to the column,

8
00:00:25,166 --> 00:00:27,100
再传向柱础与地基。
then continues to the base and foundation.

9
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:30,243
看编号二十，栌斗。
Look at number 20: the ludou, or principal block.

10
00:00:30,243 --> 00:00:35,481
它坐在柱头上，是这组斗拱下部的重要承接节点。
It sits on the column head and receives the bracket assembly.

11
00:00:35,481 --> 00:00:38,100
往上看，木件纵横相交。
Above it, timber members cross in different directions.

12
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:40,905
再看十九，华拱。
Now look at number 19: the huagong.

13
00:00:40,905 --> 00:00:43,612
它向柱外伸出，形成出跳。
It extends beyond the column to create a projection.

14
00:00:43,612 --> 00:00:48,350
屋檐的伸展，在这里开始有了清楚的结构层次。
Here the reach of the eaves begins to take a clear structural form.

15
00:00:49,350 --> 00:00:53,779
编号十七是昂。图上能看到它斜向延伸。
Number 17 is the ang, shown as an inclined member.

16
00:00:53,779 --> 00:00:56,485
注意，昂不是装饰花纹，
The ang is more than a decorative pattern:

17
00:00:56,485 --> 00:00:59,683
而是这组构件关系中的一员。
it participates in the relationships within this assembly.

18
00:01:00,683 --> 00:01:04,183
页旁直接写明：这幅示例出三跳，
The note beside the drawing explicitly describes three projections,

19
00:01:04,183 --> 00:01:06,517
由一华拱、两昂组成。
formed by one huagong and two ang members.

20
00:01:06,517 --> 00:01:11,183
跳，数的是向外挑出的层次，不是木块总数。
“Projection” counts outward-reaching stages, rather than individual blocks.

21
00:01:12,183 --> 00:01:14,188
另一把钥匙，是材。
Another key is cai, the dimensional module.

22
00:01:14,188 --> 00:01:17,085
页旁说，各部尺寸可以用材，
The note explains that dimensions can be measured in cai,

23
00:01:17,085 --> 00:01:19,981
以及它的倍数或分数来度量。
and in its multiples or fractions.

24
00:01:19,981 --> 00:01:23,100
这是一套相互协调的比例语言。
This provides a coordinated language of proportion.

25
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:27,377
下次走到古建筑前，抬头看看屋檐：
Next time you visit an old building, look up at its eaves.

26
00:01:27,377 --> 00:01:29,220
找到柱，找到栌斗，
Locate the column and the principal block,

27
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:32,906
再沿着拱和昂，追踪它向外伸出的层次。
then follow the bracket arms and ang through their outward projections.

28
00:01:32,906 --> 00:01:36,183
梁思成的一页图，就这样活了起来。
In this way, a page by Liang Sicheng comes to life.